0. there should be an action::Write that holds Buffer and Offset info. When it is time to do a compute pass or render pass. Find action::Writes that touch each other 
on the buffer so they can be executed together. There could be a chance to track what writes happen most frequently so they can be moved next to each other.


1. Make node type that does not cash results and reads its stems on every solve. This is needed so it is up to date with stems that had write_passive used on them.
2. I could keep Hedge { buffer, stem } or use Vec<ComputeCommand>. But the second option will cause unneeded recompute unless 
    sections could be marked is a number so the encoder submitter knows to skip those sections
3. Swap the names Gate and Ploy
4. builder with #[build(push_s)] and #[build(push_es)] that makes push method with "s" or "es" removed. This builder
    can be called Make and it also creates a builder that starts with the owned pattern. MyStructMaker and MyStructBuilder
5. For gpu action pack, each action can have a u64 id that only changes if it is regenerated. This tells the list builder 
    that it does not have to traverse futher down the graph that way. It only needs to save the copy of this new graph
6. make Leaf<Grc<T>> type alias
7. make Node type that uses Arc<T> instead of Arc<RwLock<T>> for edge
8. Mech should provide methods to create dispatch graph with given pipeline and such. should not manually provide BindGroupLayout and Pipeline every time because Mech already has this

